<title>FRANCE: French consumer spending fell 1.5 pct in Sept.</title>
<headline>French consumer spending fell 1.5 pct in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE gave the following seasonally adjusted figures for household spending on manufactured goods in billions of 1980 francs:</p>
<p>					    Sept   Aug    July    Sept 95</p>
<p> Total				   59.67  60.60   58.62     57.33</p>
<p> Total change (pct v pvs month)   -1.5    3.4    -0.4	 4.1</p>
<p> Retail sector			 37.04  39.21   38.74     38.48</p>
<p> Durables				20.19  19.30   17.58     16.76</p>
<p> Textiles, leather		   10.30  11.50   11.50     11.42</p>
<p> Other				   29.17  29.80   29.54     29.15</p>
<p>It gave the following percentage changes (month-on-month unless stated)</p>
<p>					    Sept   Aug    July  Sept yr/yr</p>
<p> Total				   -1.5    3.4    -0.4	  4.1</p>
<p> Retail sector			 -5.6    1.2    -0.4	 -3.8</p>
<p> Durables				 4.7    9.8    -0.9	 20.5</p>
<p>   of which cars		     18.8   18.4    -1.1	 61.1</p>
<p>   household equip		   -6.3    3.9    -0.7	 -3.5</p>
<p> Textiles, leather		  -10.5    0.0    -0.5	 -9.9</p>
<p> Other				   -2.1    0.9    -0.1	  0.1</p>
<p>NOTE - INSEE said on September 26 that consumer spending fell 0.6 percent in July and rose 3.0 percent in August.</p>
<p>INSEE said the number of foreign and French cars sold in France in September was a seasonally adjusted 248,100 after 204,380 in August.</p>
<p>In the third quarter, car sales rose 22.4 percent after dropping 7.2 percent in the second quarter.</p>
<p>Consumer spending on manufactured goods in the third quarter rose 2.6 percent compared to a 1.5 percent drop in the previous quarter, INSEE said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
